  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "s01-bench-paints-no-glyphs",
      "boundaryId": "s01-foundation",
      "criterionIds": [
        "PERF-1",
        "PERF-5"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Resolved.** The cause was that `gpui_platform`'s `bench-support` did not enable `font-kit`, so macOS benches drew with `NoopTextSystem`. `bench-support` now enables `font-kit`.\n\nThe recaptured baseline paints glyphs:\n- `still-frame/off`: 7,766 primitives a frame (was 60).\n- `scroll-child-view`: 120 a frame (was 31).\n- `hover-sweep`: 310 a frame (was 80).\n\nEvery text scenario's `expect` now applies `drawn_per_frame`, which is shared by the bench and the attribution group.\n\nThe scroll scenarios' floor has since been raised to 60 primitives a frame (86441c0), above their 31 row backgrounds, so each of them now fails on its own if the glyphs are missing.",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
