    {
      "id": "s01-hover-fix-off-path-contract",
      "boundaryId": "s01-foundation",
      "criterionIds": [
        "FM-2",
        "OR-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Resolved.** FM-2, the d-switches invariants and `docs/fast-mode.md` (\"Cached views and hovers\") now declare the cached-view hover dependency as gpux behaviour in every mode.\n\nThe one-frame lag is gone: `paint_view` notes a replay whose hovers changed (`note_stale_replay`), and `Window::draw` draws the frame again before it is shown (`redraw_stale_replays` followed by a second `draw_frame`). I checked the side effects of the discarded first frame: snapshot requests are not drained, and the focus diff, arena clear and input handler are idempotent.\n\nThe regression test `cached_view_drops_its_hover_in_the_frame_an_overlay_covers_it` exercises the covered case. The oracle now has `CoverCells` (an occluding overlay over the first grid row) and `HoverCell`, and it compares the first frame after each step (`set_draw_on_flush(false)`).",
      "regressionRefs": [
