    {
      "id": "s01-stale-redraw-notifies-observers",
      "boundaryId": "s01-foundation",
      "criterionIds": [
        "FM-2"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Resolved (86441c0).** `redraw_stale_replays(&mut Window)` now marks each stale view and its ancestors with `Window::mark_view_dirty`, which walks the rendered frame's dispatch tree into `window.dirty_views`. It no longer uses the invalidator, `Effect::Notify` or the platform waker.\n\n`dirty_views` is cleared during the first draw and not reset when the second `draw_frame` starts. So the second draw rebuilds those views, because `prepaint_view` checks `!window.dirty_views.contains`.\n\nThe overlay regression test now registers `cx.observe(&cell, ..)` and asserts, after `run_until_parked`, that the observer never ran.",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "gpux",
          "path": "crates/gpui/src/fast/dependencies.rs",
          "symbol": "redraw_stale_replays"
        },
